<title>USA: TABLE - Genzyme General Q2 net increases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Genzyme General Q2 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended   Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				 June 30,		   June 30,</p>
<p>			  1997	   1996	   1997	  1996</p>
<p>Revenue	    147,614	113,988	292,220     225,771</p>
<p>Acquisition restructuring costs</p>
<p>			   ---	  1,465	    ---	 1,465</p>
<p>Equity in net loss of unconsolidated subsidiaries</p>
<p>			 (783)	(1,121)	  (853)     (2,058)</p>
<p>Gain on investment   ---	  1,711	    ---	 1,711</p>
<p>Net income attributable to Genzyme General Stock</p>
<p>		     $23,283	$20,284	$44,521     $39,318</p>
<p>Per Genzyme General Common Share:</p>
<p>Net income per common and common equivalent share</p>
<p>			 $0.30	  $0.27	  $0.57	 $0.54</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding</p>
<p>			78,130	 73,908	 78,184	72,880</p>
<p>Net income per common share assuming full dilution</p>
<p>			 $0.30	  $0.27	  $0.57	 $0.53</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding diluted</p>
<p>			78,791	 73,934	 78,514	74,300</p>
<p>			 (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: At the end of the quarter, Genzyme Corp declared a stock dividend of 2.6 million designated shares of Genzyme Tissue Repair common stock to Genzyme General shareholders.  Of the 2.6 million shares, about 400,000 were reserved for issuance upon exercise of Genzyme General stock options and warrants outstanding on the record date.</p>
